course: dictionary
lesson: 4172
title: Big G, small g
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and a capital letter is a clue. «God» with a capital G is a name. Many religions, such as Christianity, Judaism and Islam, use it for the one being they believe made and rules the world. A name like this is a proper noun, so it always starts with a capital letter.
explain: «A god» with a small g is a powerful being in myths and some religions, like the Greek god Zeus or the Norse god Thor. Read the words around it to decide. «The ancient Greeks had many gods who ruled the sea and the sky.» Many gods in myths means the small g meaning, not the single name.
explain: Some people also use god as a joke. If a friend says, «Our goalkeeper is a god», they mean he is admired very much, not that he is a powerful being. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does it still make sense?
fact: «God» with a capital G is the name for the one being that many religions believe made and rules the world.
fact: «A god» with a small g is a powerful being in myths and some religions.
fact: Gods in myths often have special powers and rule over things like the sea, thunder or the sun.
fact: «Oh my God» is an exclamation that some people find rude, so many say «oh my gosh» instead.
fact: A person admired very much may be called a god in a joke, which only means they are admired.
exercise: «The kingdom of God is like a tiny mustard seed that grows into a large plant where birds nest.» In this sentence, what does God with a capital G name? | *The one being that many religions believe made and rules the world | A very good football player | A small seed | A Greek god of thunder
exercise: Which of these is a small g god from myths? | Gosh | *Zeus | Mashallah | God
exercise: Nadia says, «He is a god at maths!» What does it mean? | He made the world | *He is admired very much | He is a powerful being in myths | He rules the sea
test: What do many people say instead of «oh my God»? | *oh my gosh | oh my gross | oh my goat | oh my ghost
test: Why is «God» written with a capital letter in «the kingdom of God»? | It is a joke about admired people | *It is a name for the one being many religions believe made and rules the world | It is the start of a sentence | It means a small myth god
exam: Which meaning fits the word god in «the Norse god Thor»? | A kind of sea creature | *A powerful being in myths | A name for the one being many religions believe made the world | A person admired in a joke
